# No pattern here ends in a slash. A trailing slash matches a directory and nothing else, so the
# day a build output is replaced by a symlink to one, the pattern stops matching and the link is
# tracked. That is exactly how the kernel/out link came back into the tree through a merge.
**/target
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
/.cache
/.idea
/.vscode
.DS_Store
*.profraw
*.profdata
*.snap.new
coverage
/result
benchmarks/results
/fuzz/artifacts
/fuzz/corpus

# Built guest-kernel artifacts, sources, and build trees (see kernel/README.md)
kernel/out
